N2  - OBJECTIVE: Examine the validity of self-reported use of reduced fat and reduced salt foods., DESIGN: Compare data collected in a food frequency questionnaire with supermarket sales data and food supply data., SETTING: Rural Australia., SUBJECTS: Four hundred and fifty-three respondents from an original sample of 1616 randomly-selected residents., INTERVENTIONS: Community health campaign to reduce cardiovascular disease., RESULTS: Reported use of reduced fat and reduced salt foods was greater than store sales and milk deliveries of these products., CONCLUSIONS: External data did not support the validity of self-reported use of these products.
