N2  - The effect of a fat-modified reduction diet with predominantly butter (diet T) respectively margarine (diet P) on the lipid metabolism was studied. The study was carried out on 30 subjects over two periods each lasting 21 days. An improvement of serum cholesterol and -triglycerides, LDL- and VLDL-cholesterol was found regardless of the diet. The proportion of HDL in serum cholesterol increased, the atherogenic index was improved.
